course: dictionary
lesson: 10453
title: Trusted: someone you can rely on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Trusted can be an adjective or a verb. As an adjective, it describes someone who is believed to be honest, safe and reliable. «If you lose your key, do not climb in through a window; call a parent or go to a trusted neighbour.» The neighbour is someone you know well and feel safe with, so trusted tells you they are a safe person to go to.
explain: Trusted is also the past of the verb trust. «Yesterday Mia trusted her brother to keep the secret» means she believed he would be honest and do the right thing. To find out which meaning you need, look at the words around it: an adjective describes a person or thing, while a verb tells you what someone did.
explain: In safety lessons, a trusted adult is a grown-up you know well and feel safe with, such as a parent, teacher, school counsellor or relative. «The second kind you always tell a trusted adult.» Check your meaning by swapping it in: «ask a safe, reliable adult» still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Trusted is an adjective when it describes a person: a trusted adult.
fact: Trusted is also the past of the verb trust: trust, trusts, trusted, trusting.
fact: «Trusted» as an adjective means believed to be honest, safe and reliable.
fact: «Trusted» as a verb means believed someone would be honest or do what is right.
fact: Useful phrases are trusted adult, trusted friend and trusted with. Have more than one trusted adult.
exercise: «If you lose your key, do not climb in through a window; call a parent or go to a trusted neighbour.» What does trusted mean in this sentence? | *A neighbour you know well and feel safe with | A neighbour who is very tall | A neighbour who has lost their key | A neighbour who lives far away
exercise: Which of these is a trusted adult in the lessons? | A stranger in the street who offers you a sweet | A person who asks you to keep a secret from your family | *A parent or a school counsellor | Any adult you have never met
exercise: Yesterday Mia ___ her brother to keep the secret. Which word fits? | trusting | trust | *trusted | trusts
test: Which phrase means a grown-up you can rely on to keep you safe? | trusts a story | trusted with a bike | *trusted adult | trusting shoes
test: In «have more than one trusted adult», what part of speech is trusted? | adverb | *adjective | noun | verb
exam: In «If you don't know what a word means, ask a trusted adult or look it up», what does trusted tell us about the adult? | They are very old and wise | They own a dictionary | *They are safe and reliable, so you can go to them for help | They must be paid for their time
